{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Resilience Activation — Coping Outcome Dynamics\"\n",
        "format: html\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## What This Code Does\n",
        "\n",
        "This demo varies challenge and hindrance inputs across [0, 1] at three neighbour affect levels (−0.5, 0.0, +0.5) to show how coping probability, resilience effects, and resource costs respond to the challenge/hindrance balance.\n",
        "\n",
        "The theory predicts: coping probability increases with the challenge/hindrance ratio; neighbour affect modulates this curve (positive neighbours raise odds, negative neighbours lower them); successful coping reduces stress and boosts affect; failure does the reverse.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Setup"
      ],
      "id": "01a49569"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: setup\n",
        "import os\n",
        "import sys\n",
        "import pathlib\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "from numpy.random import Generator, PCG64\n",
        "\n",
        "demos_dir = pathlib.Path(os.getcwd())\n",
        "project_root = demos_dir.parents[2]\n",
        "sys.path.insert(0, str(project_root))\n",
        "\n",
        "from src.python.phases.resilience_activation import run_phase"
      ],
      "id": "setup",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 1: Sweep Challenge, Hindrance, and Neighbour Affect\n",
        "\n",
        "This 3D sweep (30×30×3 = 2,700 runs) explores the full parameter space of the resilience activation phase. Each run records coping probability, success/failure outcome, resilience effect, delta stress, delta affect, and resource cost."
      ],
      "id": "56b1f8a6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: sweep\n",
        "NEIGHBOR_LEVELS = [-0.5, 0.0, 0.5]\n",
        "N_CH, N_HI = 30, 30\n",
        "\n",
        "base_state = {\n",
        "    \"affect\": 0.0, \"resilience\": 0.5, \"current_stress\": 0.3,\n",
        "    \"baseline_resilience\": 0.5, \"stress_controllability\": 0.5,\n",
        "    \"stress_overload\": 0.5, \"volatility\": 0.5, \"recent_stress_intensity\": 0.1,\n",
        "    \"stress_momentum\": 0.0, \"resources\": 0.5,\n",
        "    \"protective_factors\": {\"social_support\": 0.5, \"family_support\": 0.5,\n",
        "                           \"formal_intervention\": 0.5, \"psychological_capital\": 0.5},\n",
        "    \"consecutive_hindrances\": 0.0, \"stress_breach_count\": 0, \"support_boost\": 0.0,\n",
        "}\n",
        "base_config = {\"base_resource_cost\": 0.1}\n",
        "records = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for neighbor_affects in NEIGHBOR_LEVELS:\n",
        "    for challenge in np.linspace(0, 1, N_CH):\n",
        "        for hindrance in np.linspace(0, 1, N_HI):\n",
        "            rng = Generator(PCG64(42))\n",
        "            state = dict(base_state)\n",
        "            state[\"challenge\"], state[\"hindrance\"] = challenge, hindrance\n",
        "            config = dict(base_config)\n",
        "            config[\"neighbor_affects\"] = [neighbor_affects]\n",
        "            out = run_phase(state, config, rng)\n",
        "            obs = out[\"observation\"]\n",
        "            records.append({\n",
        "                \"challenge\": challenge, \"hindrance\": hindrance,\n",
        "                \"neighbor_affect\": neighbor_affects,\n",
        "                \"coping_probability\": obs[\"coping_probability\"],\n",
        "                \"coped_successfully\": int(obs[\"coped_successfully\"]),\n",
        "                \"resilience_effect\": obs[\"resilience_effect\"],\n",
        "                \"delta_stress\": obs[\"delta_stress\"],\n",
        "                \"delta_affect\": obs[\"delta_affect\"],\n",
        "                \"resource_cost\": obs[\"resource_cost\"],\n",
        "            })\n",
        "\n",
        "df = pd.DataFrame(records)\n",
        "print(f\"Generated {len(df)} data points\")"
      ],
      "id": "sweep",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 2: Correlogram — Coping Outcome Patterns\n",
        "\n",
        "The 8×8 PairGrid below is coloured by coping outcome (green = success, red = failure)."
      ],
      "id": "70d89d63"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-correlogram\n",
        "vars_ = [\"challenge\", \"hindrance\", \"neighbor_affect\", \"coping_probability\",\n",
        "         \"resilience_effect\", \"delta_stress\", \"delta_affect\", \"resource_cost\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "g = sns.PairGrid(df, vars=vars_, hue=\"coped_successfully\",\n",
        "                 palette={0: \"#e74c3c\", 1: \"#2ecc71\"}, diag_sharey=False)\n",
        "g.map_upper(sns.scatterplot, s=4, alpha=0.3)\n",
        "g.map_lower(sns.scatterplot, s=4, alpha=0.3)\n",
        "g.map_diag(sns.kdeplot, fill=True)\n",
        "g.add_legend(title=\"Coped\", bbox_to_anchor=(1.05, 0.5), loc=\"center left\")\n",
        "plt.suptitle(\"Resilience Activation — Coping Outcome Correlogram\", y=1.02, fontsize=13)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-correlogram",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## What We See\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Coping probability** rises with the challenge/hindrance ratio. Pure challenge gives near-certain coping; pure hindrance gives near-zero coping.\n",
        "- **Neighbour affect** shifts the curve: supportive networks (positive affect) improve coping odds; toxic networks (negative affect) reduce them.\n",
        "- **Delta stress and affect**: successful coping (green) reduces stress and improves affect; failed coping (red) does the reverse.\n",
        "- **Resilience effect** is proportional to the challenge/hindrance gap, moderated by success.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Why This Matters for the Simulation\n",
        "\n",
        "Resilience activation is where cognitive appraisal translates into a coping outcome. This phase determines whether stress events escalate or resolve, directly feeding into the resource allocation and buffering phases. The neighbour affect modulation implements the social contagion mechanism: an agent embedded in a supportive network copes better than an isolated or negatively surrounded one."
      ],
      "id": "67e32c8e"
    }
  ],
